<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 198)</h2>
<p><b>Fixed: single-key shortcuts going dead after you'd typed anywhere.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Once you'd used any text field — a note, a comment, the look filter — that field kept the keyboard, and <b>clicking back on the picture didn't take it back</b>. Every single-letter shortcut then typed silently into that field instead of doing its job.</li>
<li><b>I and O were the ones you'd notice</b>, because setting loop in/out had no menu equivalent to fall back on. Space, stepping and most others did.</li>
<li>Clicking the image now returns the keyboard to the viewer, and closing a floating panel hands it back too.</li>
<li>Loop in/out also gained menu shortcuts — <b>⌥⌘I</b> and <b>⌥⌘O</b> — which work regardless of what has focus.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
